&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Radix supplies the modal interaction model and connects the title and description. The iframe gives the document a separate styling context; the surrounding Tailwind utilities cannot accidentally restyle its headings or captions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Configure Motion Around the Artifact
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the complete CSS configuration and micro-interaction:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"tailwindcss"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.preview-shell&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;container-type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;inline-size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.preview-layout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;display&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;grid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nl"&gt;gap&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@container&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;min-width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;48rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;.preview-layout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;grid-template-columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;minmax&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1fr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;12rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;align-items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@keyframes&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;preview-enter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;opacity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;translateY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.5rem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;to&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;opacity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;transform&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;translateY&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@media&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;prefers-reduced-motion&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;no-preference&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nc"&gt;.preview-dialog&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data-state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"open"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;animation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;preview-enter&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;160ms&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ease-out&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;both&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The container query responds to available dialog space rather than assuming the browser viewport describes the component's layout. The entrance animation never changes the iframe's document.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The Trade-offs Are Intentional
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This preview is static. Its empty sandbox disables scripts, so it cannot faithfully preview a document that depends on JavaScript-driven animation. That limitation is preferable to silently executing arbitrary generated code inside the application's trust boundary. A scripted preview needs a separately designed isolation policy.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Likewise, &lt;code&gt;aspect-video&lt;/code&gt; describes the preview box, not a guaranteed export resolution. For pixel-sensitive work, render the document at its exact production viewport and scale that surface for inspection. Otherwise, line wrapping can differ between preview and export.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sandbox also does not make HTML network-isolated. External images and styles can still create requests. Use controlled assets and an appropriate content security policy when documents are untrusted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before adoption, test keyboard entry, Escape, focus restoration, reduced motion, and representative documents with a screen reader. Radix handles the outer dialog; it cannot repair inaccessible content inside the iframe.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The architectural payoff is modest but important: Hyperframes receives a document, not a screenshot of your application. Preview improvements remain interface changes instead of becoming accidental changes to the video.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  The Isolation Dilemma
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The empty sandbox solves the trust boundary problem but creates a fidelity gap. If your video document legitimately requires scripted animation—timed transitions, chart rendering, dynamic text layout—this preview cannot show it. The alternative, enabling scripts, means previewing untrusted or generated HTML inside your application's security context.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How are you solving scripted preview safely? Separate worker context? Sandboxed subprocess? Different trust model entirely? I would value hearing how production teams are navigating this trade-off."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When building with Next.js App Router, it's tempting to add "use client" to a page as soon as one component needs state or event handlers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But that decision can affect the client-side module graph and the JavaScript the browser needs to load.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A more deliberate approach is to separate server-side responsibilities from browser-dependent interactions.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, a product page might use:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Server Component for fetching and displaying product information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Client Component for selecting product variations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Client Component for cart interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Server Components for related product content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The exact boundaries depend on the application's needs. Server Components aren't automatically better for every situation, and Client Components aren't inherently bad.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The important thing is to understand what each component needs to do.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I covered the differences, common misconceptions, composition patterns, and practical decision-making in my latest article:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React Server Components vs. Client Components: How to Choose the Right Boundary&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Read the full article on Medium: [&lt;a href="https://medium.com/@md-abu-noman/react-server-components-vs-client-components-how-to-choose-the-right-boundary-975141351036?sharedUserId=md-abu-noman" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://medium.com/@md-abu-noman/react-server-components-vs-client-components-how-to-choose-the-right-boundary-975141351036?sharedUserId=md-abu-noman&lt;/a&gt;]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Question for the community: What's your approach to deciding where "use client" belongs in a Next.js application?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What carries over
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;React concept&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Angular equivalent&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;How it helps you transition&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Component‑based UI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Angular components (&lt;code&gt;@Component&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You already think in terms of isolated UI pieces; the syntax changes but the mental model stays the same.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;JSX → Template syntax&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Angular HTML templates with binding syntax (&lt;code&gt;{{ }}&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[prop]&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;(event)&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The idea of declarative UI is identical; you just move the markup out of JavaScript.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;State management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Services + RxJS or NgRx&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your experience with Redux or Context translates to Angular services (singleton providers) and reactive streams.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hooks → Lifecycle hooks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;ngOnInit&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ngOnChanges&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ngOnDestroy&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The lifecycle concept is the same; you just implement methods on the component class instead of calling functions.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Props → @Input / @Output&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;@Input()&lt;/code&gt; for inbound data, &lt;code&gt;@Output()&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;EventEmitter&lt;/code&gt; for outbound events&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Passing data down and emitting events up works the same way, just with decorators.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Virtual DOM diffing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Angular’s change detection (default &lt;code&gt;CheckAlways&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You no longer write a diff algorithm, but you still benefit from Angular’s efficient rendering.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing libraries&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Jasmine/Karma (or Jest) + Angular TestBed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your testing mindset (unit + integration) carries over; the APIs differ but the patterns are familiar.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLI scaffolding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;ng generate component&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ng serve&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The CLI-driven workflow you love in &lt;code&gt;create‑react‑app&lt;/code&gt; is even richer in Angular.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CSS modules / Scoped styles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Component‑level style encapsulation (&lt;code&gt;encapsulation: ViewEncapsulation.Emulated&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Styles stay scoped to the component, reducing global leakage.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environment variables&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;environment.ts&lt;/code&gt; files&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The concept of build‑time configuration is the same; you just import from &lt;code&gt;src/environments&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What's new
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Small task: toggle a boolean on button click
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React (function component, hooks)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Toggle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setOn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setOn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'ON'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'OFF'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Angular (component class, template)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Component&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'@angular/core'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@Component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;selector&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'app-toggle'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;template&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`
    &amp;lt;button (click)="toggle()"&amp;gt;
      {{ on ? 'ON' : 'OFF' }}
    &amp;lt;/button&amp;gt;
  `&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ToggleComponent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;toggle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


  What changed and why
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;File structure&lt;/strong&gt; – Angular splits logic (&lt;code&gt;.ts&lt;/code&gt;) and markup (&lt;code&gt;template&lt;/code&gt; or separate &lt;code&gt;.html&lt;/code&gt;) by default, whereas React co‑locates them in JSX.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;State handling&lt;/strong&gt; – No &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;; you use plain class properties. Change detection runs automatically after the click handler finishes.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Event binding&lt;/strong&gt; – Angular uses the &lt;code&gt;(event)&lt;/code&gt; syntax in the template, not a JSX prop.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Decorator metadata&lt;/strong&gt; – &lt;code&gt;@Component&lt;/code&gt; tells Angular how to compile the class; React has no equivalent decorator.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Other notable differences:  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Dependency injection&lt;/strong&gt; – Angular injects services via constructor parameters (&lt;code&gt;constructor(private api: ApiService) {}&lt;/code&gt;), while React typically uses context or custom hooks.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Routing&lt;/strong&gt; – Angular’s &lt;code&gt;RouterModule&lt;/code&gt; provides a declarative route configuration (&lt;code&gt;{ path: 'home', component: HomeComponent }&lt;/code&gt;). React Router uses JSX &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Route&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; elements.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forms&lt;/strong&gt; – Angular offers Template‑driven (&lt;code&gt;ngModel&lt;/code&gt;) and Reactive (&lt;code&gt;FormGroup&lt;/code&gt;) APIs; React relies on controlled components or libraries like Formik.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Observables&lt;/strong&gt; – RxJS is baked into Angular; you’ll see &lt;code&gt;Observable&lt;/code&gt; streams for HTTP, events, and state. React can use RxJS but it’s not part of the core.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Common pitfalls
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Forgetting to unsubscribe&lt;/strong&gt; – Angular components stay alive until destroyed. If you subscribe to an &lt;code&gt;Observable&lt;/code&gt; inside a component, always &lt;code&gt;ngOnDestroy&lt;/code&gt; and call &lt;code&gt;unsubscribe()&lt;/code&gt; or use the &lt;code&gt;async&lt;/code&gt; pipe.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Mixing template syntax&lt;/strong&gt; – Using both &lt;code&gt;[property]&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;{{ }}&lt;/code&gt; for the same value can cause “Expression has changed after it was checked” errors. Stick to one binding style per property.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Over‑using &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; – TypeScript is mandatory in Angular projects; resist the urge to fall back to &lt;code&gt;any&lt;/code&gt;. Define interfaces for inputs, API responses, and service contracts.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ignoring change detection strategy&lt;/strong&gt; – The default &lt;code&gt;CheckAlways&lt;/code&gt; can cause performance regressions in large apps. Consider &lt;code&gt;ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush&lt;/code&gt; for immutable data flows, similar to React’s memoization.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Assuming Angular CLI mirrors CRA&lt;/strong&gt; – Commands differ (&lt;code&gt;ng generate&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ng build --prod&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ng test&lt;/code&gt;). Read the Angular CLI docs instead of mapping CRA flags one‑to‑one.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Your 30‑day plan
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Week 1 – Foundations
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install the Angular CLI (&lt;code&gt;npm i -g @angular/cli&lt;/code&gt;) and generate a new workspace: &lt;code&gt;ng new my‑angular‑app&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore the generated folder structure (&lt;code&gt;src/app&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;src/environments&lt;/code&gt;).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a simple “Hello World” component using &lt;code&gt;ng generate component hello&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read the official &lt;strong&gt;Component&lt;/strong&gt; guide; implement &lt;code&gt;@Input&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;@Output&lt;/code&gt; between a parent and child component.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mini project:&lt;/strong&gt; Create a “Todo List” with a static array of items, displaying them with &lt;code&gt;*ngFor&lt;/code&gt; and toggling completion via a button.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Week 2 – Data flow &amp;amp; services
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaffold a service (&lt;code&gt;ng generate service api&lt;/code&gt;) and inject it into a component.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Angular’s &lt;code&gt;HttpClientModule&lt;/code&gt; to fetch data from a public JSON endpoint; handle the &lt;code&gt;Observable&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;async&lt;/code&gt; pipe.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce a simple state store using a service with a &lt;code&gt;BehaviorSubject&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compare a React Context + reducer pattern with the Angular service approach.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mini project:&lt;/strong&gt; Extend the Todo app to load items from an API, add new items via a form, and persist changes in the service’s &lt;code&gt;BehaviorSubject&lt;/code&gt;.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Week 3 – Routing, forms, and testing
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up &lt;code&gt;RouterModule&lt;/code&gt; with at least three routes (&lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/about&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;/todos&lt;/code&gt;). Use lazy‑loaded modules (&lt;code&gt;ng generate module admin --route admin --module app.module&lt;/code&gt;).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement a reactive form for adding a Todo (&lt;code&gt;FormBuilder&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;FormGroup&lt;/code&gt;, validators).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write a unit test for a component using &lt;code&gt;TestBed&lt;/code&gt; and a service test with &lt;code&gt;HttpTestingController&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run end‑to‑end tests with Cypress (optional) to see how Angular’s testing stack integrates.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mini project:&lt;/strong&gt; Build a “Dashboard” page that shows a summary of Todos, navigable via the router, with a form to add new Todos.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Week 4 – Advanced patterns &amp;amp; polishing
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiment with &lt;code&gt;ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush&lt;/code&gt; on a performance‑critical component; measure change detection cycles with &lt;code&gt;ngDevMode&lt;/code&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add a global error handler (&lt;code&gt;ErrorHandler&lt;/code&gt; implementation) and a toast service for user feedback.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore Angular Material: install &lt;code&gt;@angular/material&lt;/code&gt;, add a toolbar and a dialog for editing a Todo.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize the build for production (&lt;code&gt;ng build --configuration production&lt;/code&gt;) and deploy to a static host (e.g., Netlify).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capstone project:&lt;/strong&gt; Refactor the Todo Dashboard into a small “Task Manager” app with routing, lazy modules, reactive forms, Material UI, and a shared state service. Deploy it and verify the production bundle size.  &lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  How much TypeScript do I need to know?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You need a solid grasp of interfaces, classes, and generics; Angular’s templates are type‑checked against component class definitions, so the compiler will guide you.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Can I still use JSX in Angular?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. Angular’s template syntax is HTML‑based and compiled by the Angular compiler; JSX is exclusive to React (or frameworks that adopt it).  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Do I have to adopt RxJS for every async operation?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not mandatory, but most Angular APIs (HTTP, router events, forms) return &lt;code&gt;Observable&lt;/code&gt;s. Learning the basic operators (&lt;code&gt;map&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;switchMap&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;takeUntil&lt;/code&gt;) will pay off quickly.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Is Angular slower than React because of its change detection?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Angular’s default change detection is efficient for most apps. With &lt;code&gt;OnPush&lt;/code&gt; and immutable data patterns you can achieve performance comparable to React’s virtual DOM diffing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Keep going
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;See what already transfers:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://switchbyskill.com/switch-check?pair=react-to-angular&amp;amp;utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=community&amp;amp;utm_campaign=blog-30-day-plan&amp;amp;utm_content=react-developer-learning-angular-what-carries-over-what-s-new-30" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;take the free React → Angular readiness check&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://switchbyskill.com/switch/react-to-angular" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;The full React → Angular roadmap, topic by topic&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Related: &lt;a href="https://switchbyskill.com/blog/angular-developer-learning-react-what-carries-over-what-s-new-30-day-plan" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Angular developer learning React: what carries over, what's new, 30-day plan&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Related: &lt;a href="https://switchbyskill.com/blog/react-developer-learning-next-js-what-carries-over-what-s-new-30-day-plan" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React developer learning Next.js: what carries over, what's new, 30-day plan&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published at &lt;a href="https://switchbyskill.com/blog/react-developer-learning-angular-what-carries-over-what-s-new-30-day-plan" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;switchbyskill.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Building a Telegram Mini App inside React feels straightforward: Telegram provides a native JavaScript script, developers load it, pull the user object from &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.initDataUnsafe.user&lt;/code&gt;, and render a custom storefront or checkout interface. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, relying on &lt;code&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt; for backend transactions opens a severe security vulnerability. The &lt;code&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt; object is unverified front-end state. Anyone opening your Mini App in Telegram Desktop, a browser, or a custom webview can open Developer Tools or intercept network requests to override &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.initDataUnsafe.user.id&lt;/code&gt; with any arbitrary user ID. If your React app sends that unverified &lt;code&gt;user.id&lt;/code&gt; to your backend checkout endpoint, an attacker can place orders, view private data, or deplete account balances under another user's identity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To build a secure Mini App, you must transmit the raw, untouched &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; query string to your server, verify its HMAC-SHA256 signature using your Telegram Bot Token, check the payload timestamp to block replay attacks, and only then enable native UI controls like the &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Loading the Telegram SDK and Extracting Raw initData in React
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers often choose between importing &lt;code&gt;@twa-dev/sdk&lt;/code&gt; from npm or loading the official &lt;code&gt;https://telegram.org/js/telegram-web-app.js&lt;/code&gt; script via an HTML script tag. Both expose the exact same global &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp&lt;/code&gt; object. While &lt;code&gt;@twa-dev/sdk&lt;/code&gt; provides TypeScript definitions, the underlying object is identical.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The key structural difference lies between two properties:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/code&gt;: A parsed JavaScript object containing user metadata (&lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;first_name&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;username&lt;/code&gt;). It is convenient for populating non-sensitive UI elements like profile avatars before network requests complete. &lt;strong&gt;Never use this property for API authorization.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt;: A raw, URL-encoded string generated and signed by Telegram's servers containing key-value pairs (including &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;auth_date&lt;/code&gt;). This exact string must be forwarded to your server in an HTTP header or request body.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a custom React hook that initializes the Telegram WebApp context safely, handles SSR execution environments, extracts the raw &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; string, and configures native viewport parameters.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;TelegramUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;first_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;last_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;username&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;language_code&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;WebAppInitState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;isReady&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;boolean&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;unsafeUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;TelegramUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;WebApp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTelegramWebApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;WebAppInitState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;WebAppInitState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;isReady&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;''&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;unsafeUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Ensure window.Telegram is available (prevents SSR crashes)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;typeof&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'undefined'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Telegram&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;WebApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Telegram&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;WebApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Expand app to full height inside Telegram container&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;tg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;expand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;isReady&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;unsafeUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;tg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;initDataUnsafe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;TelegramUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;tg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;state&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If a user launches your React app outside Telegram (for example, directly in Chrome during local testing), &lt;code&gt;tg.initData&lt;/code&gt; will be an empty string (&lt;code&gt;""&lt;/code&gt;). Your front-end logic must detect this state early and prevent authenticated API calls when &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; is missing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Cryptographic Backend Validation of raw initData
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To verify that &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; originated from Telegram and was not tampered with on the client, your server must implement Telegram's exact HMAC-SHA256 verification algorithm.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The validation sequence follows these strict steps:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parse the raw &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; query string into key-value pairs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extract and remove the &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt; parameter from the dataset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sort the remaining key-value pairs alphabetically by key.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Format sorted pairs into a &lt;code&gt;key=value&lt;/code&gt; format separated by newline characters (&lt;code&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;). This string is the &lt;code&gt;data_check_string&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a secret key by calculating an HMAC-SHA256 hash of your secret Bot Token, using the constant string &lt;code&gt;"WebAppData"&lt;/code&gt; as the key.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculate an HMAC-SHA256 signature of the &lt;code&gt;data_check_string&lt;/code&gt; using the generated secret key.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compare your calculated hex signature with the received &lt;code&gt;hash&lt;/code&gt; using a timing-safe equality check (&lt;code&gt;crypto.timingSafeEqual&lt;/code&gt;) to mitigate timing attacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Check the &lt;code&gt;auth_date&lt;/code&gt; unix timestamp against the current server time to reject stale payloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a production-ready Express.js middleware implementation in Node.js using native &lt;code&gt;crypto&lt;/code&gt; modules:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Request&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NextFunction&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'express'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'node:crypto'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;VerifiedRequest&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;extends&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Request&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;telegramUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;validateTelegramInitData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;botToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;maxAgeSeconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;86400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;VerifiedRequest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;NextFunction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rawInitData&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'x-telegram-init-data'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rawInitData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;401&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Missing Telegram initData header'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;URLSearchParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;rawInitData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'hash'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Missing hash parameter in initData'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="n"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;delete&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'hash'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Step 3 &amp;amp; 4: Sort alphabetically and build data_check_string&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sortedParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Array&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;keys&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sort&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;forEach&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;sortedParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;push&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`${key}=${urlParams.get(key)}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataCheckString&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;sortedParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'
'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Step 5: Compute secret key = HMAC-SHA256("WebAppData", botToken)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;secretKey&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createHmac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'sha256'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'WebAppData'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;botToken&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;digest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Step 6: Compute calculated hash = HMAC-SHA256(dataCheckString, secretKey)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;calculatedHash&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;createHmac&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'sha256'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;secretKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;update&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;dataCheckString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;digest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'hex'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Step 7: Timing-safe comparison&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;hashBuffer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Buffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'hex'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;calculatedBuffer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Buffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;calculatedHash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'hex'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;hashBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;calculatedBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;timingSafeEqual&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hashBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;calculatedBuffer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;403&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Invalid HMAC signature'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Step 8: Validate timestamp freshness (auth_date)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;authDateStr&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'auth_date'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;authDateStr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;400&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Missing auth_date'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;authDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;parseInt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;authDateStr&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;currentTime&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;floor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;currentTime&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;authDate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;maxAgeSeconds&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;res&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;403&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'InitData payload has expired'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Parse verified user payload and attach to request&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;userJson&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;urlParams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'user'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;userJson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;req&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;telegramUser&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;parse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;userJson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;next&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If an attacker modifies &lt;code&gt;user.id&lt;/code&gt; inside their local client runtime, the backend check will recalculate &lt;code&gt;calculatedHash&lt;/code&gt; against the modified &lt;code&gt;dataCheckString&lt;/code&gt;. Because the attacker does not possess your private Telegram Bot Token, their modified payload will fail the &lt;code&gt;crypto.timingSafeEqual&lt;/code&gt; comparison and trigger a 403 response.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Synchronizing React State with Native MainButton Lifecycle
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Telegram's native &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; renders outside the webview iframe directly in the native messaging client UI. Managing &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; state inside React components requires strict event cleanup and asynchronous state handling.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Common implementation errors include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attaching event listeners inside &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; without cleaning them up on unmount, causing duplicate order submissions when components re-render.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Showing &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; before backend validation completes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calling &lt;code&gt;WebApp.ready()&lt;/code&gt; before React finishes initial UI rendering, causing visual flickers during load.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a component pattern for a secure Checkout flow. The &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; is only configured after confirming client initialization, and network actions execute with visual feedback indicators on the native button.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'react'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useTelegramWebApp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'./useTelegramWebApp'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;interface&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CartItem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SecureCheckout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;FC&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;isReady&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTelegramWebApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;isProcessing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setIsProcessing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;orderStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setOrderStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;CartItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'item_101'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Premium Subscription'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;15.00&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;handleCheckout&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useCallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;isProcessing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setIsProcessing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;MainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;showProgress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'/api/checkout'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'POST'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Content-Type'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'application/json'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'X-Telegram-Init-Data'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="n"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cart&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Checkout request failed'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

      &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setOrderStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Order successfully processed!'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;MainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;hide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HapticFeedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;notificationOccurred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'success'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setOrderStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sb"&gt;`Error: ${err.message}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;HapticFeedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;notificationOccurred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'error'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;finally&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setIsProcessing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;MainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;hideProgress&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;isProcessing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;isReady&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mainButton&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;MainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Configure initial button state&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;mainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'PAY $15.00'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;mainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;enable&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;mainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;show&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Bind event handler&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;mainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;handleCheckout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Notify Telegram that UI layout is rendered and stable&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;ready&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

    &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Cleanup listener on component unmount&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;mainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;offClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;handleCheckout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="n"&gt;mainButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;hide&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;isReady&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;webApp&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;handleCheckout&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;isReady&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Loading&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Telegram&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;initData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Please&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;open&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;this&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;application&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;inside&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Telegram&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;style&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;padding&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'16px'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Your&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Cart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;cart&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
          &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;strong&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;${item.price.toFixed(2)}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;strong&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
        &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
      &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;orderStatus&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;orderStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


  Production Edge Cases and Security Architecture
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When running Telegram Mini Apps in production environments, implement the following security layers:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Replay Attack Prevention
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;auth_date&lt;/code&gt; field in &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; specifies when Telegram generated the authentication payload. A malicious user could copy a valid &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; string from network logs and resend it days later. Setting &lt;code&gt;maxAgeSeconds&lt;/code&gt; (e.g., 86400 seconds for 24 hours) in your backend verification middleware ensures stale authentication signatures are rejected. For high-security transactions, convert the verified &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; into a short-lived HTTP-only JWT session cookie upon initial app boot, rather than passing raw &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; headers on every single fetch request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Initialization Race Conditions
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Never trigger &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.ready()&lt;/code&gt; inside your index HTML header or before React component trees finish mounting. Calling &lt;code&gt;ready()&lt;/code&gt; tells Telegram's native container to hide the loading overlay. If your app calls &lt;code&gt;ready()&lt;/code&gt; before React renders its DOM node, the user experiences a white flash or unstyled screen layout. Call &lt;code&gt;ready()&lt;/code&gt; inside a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; after your state setup and &lt;code&gt;MainButton&lt;/code&gt; listeners are attached.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Local Development and Mocking
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because &lt;code&gt;window.Telegram.WebApp.initData&lt;/code&gt; is empty in standard web browsers, developers often hardcode mock user objects in React state during development. Avoid hardcoding mock users directly into production bundles. Use environment variables to toggle mock modes, and isolate mock behaviors so production builds strictly enforce non-empty &lt;code&gt;initData&lt;/code&gt; signatures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you are expanding your Telegram bot infrastructure or building complex full-stack Mini Apps, consult &lt;a href="https://botservice.biz" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;BotCreator&lt;/a&gt; — studio that ships Telegram bots / Mini Apps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Folio is a free online PDF studio: 41 tools to merge, split, compress, convert to and from Word, Excel, PowerPoint and images, OCR, sign, protect and redact, plus a full page editor that can change the text already in a PDF. There is no account and no sign-up. Files are processed on Folio's own server and deleted after 6 hours (24 hours for documents open in the editor).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://folio.niranjand.in" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Open Folio&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The problem
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Everyday PDF jobs are small: join two files, shrink one to fit an upload limit, turn a scan into searchable text, sign a form. I wanted one place that does all of them without an account or a payment step, and an editor that changes the words already on the page instead of only drawing new ones on top.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Decisions that shaped it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;One tool is one Python function. Every tool is &lt;code&gt;run(inputs, options, out_dir)&lt;/code&gt; that returns the output files, registered with its title, category, accepted file types and an option schema. The React front end draws each tool's options from that schema, so adding a tool means one function and one registry entry, with no new page to build. Workflows reuse the same registry: the files one step produces are the inputs of the next, so "make searchable, then compress" is just two entries in a list.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Use proven engines, and write the glue. PyMuPDF does parsing, rendering, editing and redaction. pikepdf (qpdf underneath) handles encryption and repair, pdf2docx keeps tables and layout when going to Word, pymupdf4llm keeps headings, lists and links when going to Markdown, and Tesseract does OCR with English, Hindi and Tamil installed. On the server, LibreOffice converts Office files and a headless Chromium prints web pages to PDF.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Edit the real text, not a layer over it. The server renders each page as an image and sends back every text span with its box, font, size and colour. When you click a span and type, the old text is removed with a redaction that leaves images alone, and the new text is written into the same box. Fonts embedded in PDFs are usually subsets that lack the letters you are adding, so Folio looks up the same family among the installed fonts, with metric-compatible free stand-ins on the server (Liberation Sans for Arial, Carlito for Calibri). Every save is a new version of the document, so undo just goes back one.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Text inside pictures gets the same treatment. Scans and screenshots have no text layer, so OCR reads each line, then Folio works out the font, weight and size by rendering installed fonts against the image and comparing. An edit redraws only from the first changed letter onward, with matching anti-aliasing, so the change blends in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Redaction removes, it does not cover. Matching text is taken out of the file itself, with presets for email addresses, phone numbers and card numbers, and the metadata can be wiped too. A black box drawn over text that is still underneath is not a redaction.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;The website says only what the server can do. The same code also runs as a local app on a PC. The website leaves out what its server can't serve: Translate PDF needs a translation model the server doesn't have, so the site lists 41 tools instead of 42, and the pages that manage a computer's own folders, AI models and saved details are switched off there and kept out of search. The privacy line, the tool count and the hours files are kept all come from one file, and the build checks the tool count against the real tool list.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Test every tool. The backend has 161 test functions covering conversions, page organising and security, editor operations, OCR quality, screenshot text editing and batch speed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Built with
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Python, FastAPI, PyMuPDF, pikepdf, Tesseract, LibreOffice, React, TypeScript, Vite, Docker&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published at &lt;a href="https://folio.niranjand.in" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;folio.niranjand.in&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://wine.equipment" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;wine.equipment&lt;/a&gt; is a catalogue of winery equipment: crushers, presses, tanks, filters, bottling lines. It also has a &lt;a href="https://wine.equipment/calculator" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;cost calculator&lt;/a&gt;. You pick how many cases a year you make, the wine type and how automated you want to be, and it gives you a budget range per production stage.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The calculator was wrong, and the page itself showed it. Below each stage's estimate it printed what listings on the site actually cost. The two numbers sat a few pixels apart and disagreed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The rule of thumb
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The estimate was a per-case rule. Each stage has a dollar-per-case range, and the result is scaled for wine type and automation:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;STAGES&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"grape-processing"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"fermentation"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;     &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;25&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"pressing"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;         &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;18&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"wine-transfer"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"filtration"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;       &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"bottling"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;         &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;autoMult&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;automation&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"manual"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.6&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;automation&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"semi-automatic"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;typeMult&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;wineType&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"red"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;wineType&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;===&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sparkling"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mf"&gt;1.5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;autoMult&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;typeMult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// estimate = volume × rate × m&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For a commercial winery that's reasonable. Equipment cost does grow with volume.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a small one it breaks. At the default setting (500 cases, red, semi-automatic) the rule priced pressing at &lt;strong&gt;$3,300 – $9,900&lt;/strong&gt;. The cheapest semi-automatic press in the catalogue was &lt;strong&gt;$24,975&lt;/strong&gt;. A winery needs at least one press whatever its volume, and a press doesn't come in a size that costs $3,300 just because you make less wine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The total came out at $20,900 – $50,050. That was roughly a quarter of what the listings said.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The fix: let the catalogue set a floor
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The data was already there. The page loaded catalogue prices per stage to show the "Listed here" line. It just wasn't used for the estimate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two changes:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Group prices by automation level, not only by stage.&lt;/strong&gt; Comparing a semi-automatic estimate to the cheapest press of &lt;em&gt;any&lt;/em&gt; kind would mix basket presses with full pneumatic lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use them as bounds.&lt;/strong&gt; A stage's range never starts below the cheapest listing at the chosen level, and never tops out below their median.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;calculateBudget&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;volume&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;wineType&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;automation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="n"&gt;catalogue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;StagePrices&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// stage -&amp;gt; { lo, hi, median } at this automation level&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;BudgetItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="no"&gt;STAGES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ruleLow&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;round&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;volume&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ruleHigh&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;round&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;volume&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;rate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;m&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;catalogue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;low&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ruleLow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;lo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ruleLow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;high&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ruleHigh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;listed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;median&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ruleHigh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;stage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;low&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;high&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;raisedToCatalogue&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;low&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ruleLow&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Everything is &lt;code&gt;Math.max&lt;/code&gt;. The catalogue can only raise a number, never lower it, so large wineries where the rule already beats the listings are untouched. Both bounds come from real listings, so there's no made-up minimum anywhere in the code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The automation level needed one more step. The &lt;code&gt;automation_level&lt;/code&gt; column holds whatever the importers wrote: &lt;code&gt;semi-automatic&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;semi-auto&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;automatic&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;fully-automatic&lt;/code&gt; and so on. The site already had a map of spellings for its filters, so the calculator reuses it rather than keeping a second list:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;automationOption&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;spellings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;entries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;AUTOMATION_VARIANTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;spellings&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;includes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;option&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;When the floor kicks in, the stage says so: "Raised to the cheapest semi-automatic machine listed". A visitor can see why the number moved and click through to that machine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What changed
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Setup&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Before&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;After&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;500 cases, red, semi-automatic&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;$20,900 – $50,050&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;$78,940 – $163,410&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;5,000 cases, red, semi-automatic&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;$209,000 – $500,500&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;$209,000 – $500,500&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The large winery doesn't move, which is the point. The tests pin both cases. One feeds in a catalogue and checks that pressing goes to $24,975 – $44,800. Another checks that 10,000 cases is exactly what the rule says.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The stage where the data said no
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Bottling didn't follow. At semi-automatic it stayed at $2,750 – $8,250, while the line under it said listings run $13,440 – $114,750.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The obvious move was to apply the same floor using every bottling listing. Then I looked at what those listings were. Nearly every priced bottling machine is an automatic line: monoblocs, rotary labellers, volumetric fillers. The one exception, the $13,440 labeller at the bottom of the range, has no automation level recorded at all. The kit a 500-case winery would actually buy, a vacuum bottle filler and a bench corker, is in the catalogue too, but without a price.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So raising the estimate would have told a small winery it needs at least $13,440 for bottling, based on machines it would never buy. The rule's $2,750 – $8,250 was the better guess. The problem was the label, which put automatic-line prices next to a semi-automatic estimate as if they were the same thing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That row now reads:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No semi-automatic machine priced here. Other levels: $13,440 – $114,750&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Same numbers, honest framing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I'd take from it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;If your page shows two numbers that disagree, one of them is a bug.&lt;/strong&gt; Users notice before you do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Check what the data actually holds before you build on it.&lt;/strong&gt; 53 of 156 listings have no automation level, and nearly every priced bottling machine was automatic. A fix that looked general only held for five stages out of six.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Prefer bounds over replacements.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;Math.max(rule, catalogue)&lt;/code&gt; kept everything that already worked and only corrected what was too low.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;When you have no comparable data, say so.&lt;/strong&gt; A clear "nothing priced at this level" is more useful than a confident number built from the wrong machines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Try it at &lt;a href="https://wine.equipment/calculator" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;wine.equipment/calculator&lt;/a&gt;, or browse the &lt;a href="https://wine.equipment/equipment" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;equipment catalogue&lt;/a&gt; by production stage. Figures there are budgeting estimates, not quotes. Only a manufacturer can price a real configuration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The PR “cleans up” a form by wrapping every event handler in &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; and every derived boolean in &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;. The commit message says “performance.” There is no profile, no skipped render that mattered, and two stale-closure bugs in the validation path.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I’ve started treating &lt;strong&gt;agent-added &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; without a stated reason as noise&lt;/strong&gt;, not as an optimization. React is not cheaper just because the call site looks official. The wrappers are extra dependencies to get wrong.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why the wrap is usually cargo cult
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The model has been trained on a lot of “always memoize callbacks passed to children” advice. Some of that advice was aimed at class components, or at a child wrapped in &lt;code&gt;memo&lt;/code&gt; that actually sits in a hot list. A one-off &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Button onClick={...}&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; in a settings page is not that situation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; also lies about cost. Memoizing a boolean &lt;code&gt;const isEmpty = items.length === 0&lt;/code&gt; is slower to think about than the comparison. Memoizing a big filtered list can be real — if the input is large and the parent renders often. That sentence should be in the PR, not implied by the hook.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stale closures show up when the dependency array omits a function or a piece of form state. The memo was added to help, and now a submit handler sees yesterday’s values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  A simple memo policy
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; by default&lt;/strong&gt; in agent PRs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Allowed&lt;/strong&gt; when the PR names the expensive child or the measured cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;memo&lt;/code&gt; on a list row&lt;/strong&gt; is a reason to stabilize props; a random button is not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Derived data first&lt;/strong&gt; — a selector or a cheap variable, then memo only if needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the team already has a lint rule (&lt;code&gt;react-hooks&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;react/no-unstable-nested-components&lt;/code&gt;), the agent should follow it, not pre-empt it with wrappers everywhere.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What to put in the prompt
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight markdown"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Do not add useMemo or useCallback unless you can name the expensive render or the memoized child that depends on referential identity.
Do not wrap simple booleans, className strings, or one-off click handlers.
If you do memoize, include the reason in the PR body and list the dependencies carefully.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In review, if the hook was not there before the bugfix, ask whether the bugfix still works with the hook removed. Many times it does.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A useful exception is a context provider that passes a large value object into a wide tree. Stabilizing &lt;em&gt;that&lt;/em&gt; value can be real work. Stabilizing a click handler on a leaf button, in the same PR, is still decoration. If the agent “also memoized the context value,” make it show the provider file and the consumers, not a blanket hook pass.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; is not a substitute for moving expensive work out of render — a filter over 20,000 rows belongs in a worker, a query library, or a precomputed index, not in a hook that still runs on the main thread the first time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Reject / send back
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reject&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A blanket “performance pass” that only adds memos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useMemo(() =&amp;gt; items.length === 0, [items])&lt;/code&gt; as decoration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A stale-closure bug introduced by a new dependency array&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Memoizing something that is immediately passed into a non-memoized host component&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accept&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A memo whose PR note names the expensive list, chart, or memoized child&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A removed memo that was already doing nothing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A real profile or render-count note, even a rough one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kucing UNJ&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;em&gt;Perkucingan di UNJ&lt;/em&gt;) adalah aplikasi web interaktif yang dirancang untuk menghubungkan mahasiswa dan pencinta kucing di lingkungan &lt;strong&gt;Universitas Negeri Jakarta (UNJ)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;🔗 &lt;strong&gt;Aplikasi Dan Website:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://kucingunj.ai.studio" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://kucingunj.ai.studio&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

